Thanks for the thorough review. Pushed 01feddc:
- both embedding tests now assert `"options" not in call_args`;
- added `test_resolve_distinct_id_precedence_and_blank_values` (precedence, blank context, explicit override, falsy `0`);
- `_resolve_distinct_id` and the OpenAI/Gemini callers use `is not None` checks, so `distinct_id` and `personless` cannot disagree for falsy ids.

I left the `capture_streaming_event` reuse for a separate change to keep this PR scoped.

This reply was drafted with an AI coding assistant (Claude); the change was tested with the OpenAI/Gemini/utils suites.
